@*
    OdsSecretSettingField — one encrypted, write-only credential in the SettingField shape
    (Odyssey Design System · components/SecretSettingField).

    THE COUNTERPART TO OdsSettingField for values the API stores but never returns. It renders
    the same .odc-sfield chrome directly rather than composing OdsSettingField, exactly as the
    design system's own SecretSettingField.jsx does: the legend carries a marker OdsSettingField
    has no slot for, and the frame takes an `unreadable` state its Bound/Error vocabulary cannot
    express. Building it from the shared classes keeps one visual definition without bending a
    component every other settings row depends on.

    It replaces OdsSecretSettingRow, which was built on OdsSettingRow — the Preferences card with
    an icon tile and a right-hand control column. That shape was never what the design specified,
    and on a System settings page made entirely of notched field blocks it read as a foreign object.

    THREE STATES, ONE FRAME, NO SHARED VOCABULARY.
      Set         a fixed-length dot mask + Replace / Clear. Fixed, because the real length is
                  itself a disclosure. Screen readers get "Value stored, hidden" — a run of
                  bullets says nothing.
      NotSet      the entry input, inline and immediately typeable. The one state with nothing to
                  protect and something to do, so it costs no click. The amber advisory names what
                  is not working meanwhile.
      Unreadable  coral outline, "Cannot be decrypted", Replace / Clear. The row the encrypted
                  store exists to make legible instead of silent: the value is present and the
                  consumer is failing closed right now, so `Affects` names what stopped — nothing
                  about the key's name tells an administrator that.

    Unreadable must never read as NotSet. An absent row is a healthy configuration; an
    undecryptable one is a fault, and the two share no colour, no glyph and no copy here.

    IT DOES NOT PARTICIPATE IN THE PAGE'S SAVE. Each field commits through its own per-key
    endpoint, immediately, on its own Save — so the page's green "Saved" never means a credential
    was written, and an in-progress edit is discarded if the search filter re-renders it away.

    THE IN-PROGRESS VALUE LIVES IN A COMPONENT-LOCAL FIELD ONLY. /settings persists its UI state
    SERVER-side through the user-preferences table — the very database this feature exists to keep
    plaintext credentials out of — so a value leaking into page state would be written to durable
    server storage and into every backup.
*@
@implements IDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<div class="@WrapperClass" id="@Id">
    <fieldset class="@FrameClass">
        <legend class="odc-sfield-legend">
            @* A real <label for> only while there is an input to point at; the rest of the time the
               frame holds a mask or a status word, and a label pointing at nothing is worse than a
               span. The actions name themselves. *@
            @if (Entering)
            {
                <label class="odc-sfield-label" id="@LabelId" for="@InputId" tabindex="-1">@Title</label>
            }
            else
            {
                <span class="odc-sfield-label" id="@LabelId" tabindex="-1">@Title</span>
            }
            @* The kind marker sits in the OUTLINE, where the bound marker lives on a numeric field:
               a derivation key is a different class of loss, and that has to be legible before the
               value's state is. As TEXT (WCAG 1.4.1), never colour alone. *@
            @if (IsDerivationKey)
            {
                <span class="odc-secret-kind"
                      title="Derivation key — its loss cannot be undone by re-issuing it">Derivation key</span>
            }
        </legend>

        <div class="odc-secret-body">
            <div class="odc-secret-val">
                @if (Entering)
                {
                    <div class="odc-secret-entry">
                        <input id="@InputId"
                               class="odc-input odc-secret-input"
                               type="@(_revealed ? "text" : "password")"
                               value="@_value"
                               placeholder="Paste or type the value"
                               maxlength="@MaxLength"
                               autocomplete="new-password"
                               spellcheck="false"
                               disabled="@(_mode == Mode.Saving)"
                               aria-invalid="@(FieldError is null ? null : "true")"
                               aria-describedby="@DescribedBy"
                               @oninput="OnValueInput"
                               @onkeydown="OnEntryKeyDown" />

                        @* Revealing is not a concession here: a mistyped relay password or API key
                           fails silently and the stored value can never be read back to check, so
                           the one moment it is legible is while it is being typed. *@
                        <button type="button"
                                class="odc-secret-eye"
                                aria-label="@(_revealed ? "Hide value" : "Show value")"
                                aria-pressed="@(_revealed ? "true" : "false")"
                                disabled="@(_value.Length == 0 || _mode == Mode.Saving)"
                                @onclick="ToggleReveal">
                            <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">@(_revealed ? "visibility_off" : "visibility")</span>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
                else if (State == SecretSettingState.Unreadable)
                {
                    <span class="odc-secret-bad">
                        <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">lock</span>
                        Cannot be decrypted
                    </span>
                }
                else if (State == SecretSettingState.Set)
                {
                    @* aria-hidden: a run of bullets says nothing. The screen-reader equivalent is the
                       sr-only line on the helper row below. *@
                    <span class="odc-secret-mask" aria-hidden="true">@MaskGlyphs</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="odc-secret-empty">Not set</span>
                }
            </div>

            <div class="odc-secret-actions">
                @if (Entering)
                {
                    @* Cancel only from a REPLACE: from NotSet the input is the field's resting state,
                       so there is nothing to return to. *@
                    @if (_mode is Mode.Editing or Mode.Saving && State != SecretSettingState.NotSet)
                    {
                        <OdsButton Variant="OdsButtonVariant.Text" OnClick="CancelAsync" Disabled="@(_mode == Mode.Saving)">
                            Cancel
                        </OdsButton>
                    }
                    <OdsButton Icon="lock"
                               Loading="@(_mode == Mode.Saving)"
                               Disabled="@(_value.Trim().Length == 0 || AsciiError is not null)"
                               OnClick="SaveAsync">Save</OdsButton>
                }
                else if (!Disabled)
                {
                    @* An unreadable row's Replace is FILLED: it is the remedy, and the row is an
                       outage rather than a setting waiting to be edited. *@
                    <OdsButton id="@ActionId"
                               Variant="@(State == SecretSettingState.Unreadable ? OdsButtonVariant.Filled : OdsButtonVariant.Outlined)"
                               Icon="autorenew"
                               OnClick="BeginEdit">Replace</OdsButton>
                    <OdsButton Variant="OdsButtonVariant.Text"
                               Icon="delete_outline"
                               Loading="@(_mode == Mode.Clearing)"
                               OnClick="OpenConfirm">Clear</OdsButton>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </fieldset>

    @* Above the helper line and never displacing it: the reader keeps the definition of the setting
       while fixing the value. Only the 400 sets aria-invalid — a 403, 429 or 503 says nothing about
       the submitted value, so marking the input invalid would tell a screen-reader user to fix a
       value that was fine.

       role="alert" is dropped while the confirmation dialog is open: this element is behind the scrim
       then, the dialog renders its own visible copy, and two live elements would speak one failure
       twice. *@
    @if (FieldError is { } fieldError)
    {
        <div class="odc-sfield-err" id="@ErrorId" role="@(_confirmOpen ? null : "alert")">@fieldError</div>
    }
    @if (_rowError is { } rowError)
    {
        <div class="odc-sfield-err" id="@RowErrorId" role="@(_confirmOpen ? null : "alert")">@rowError</div>
    }
    @if (UnreadableMessage is { } unreadableMessage)
    {
        <div class="odc-sfield-err">@unreadableMessage</div>
    }

    <div class="odc-sfield-help" id="@HelpId">
        @if (State == SecretSettingState.Set)
        {
            <span class="sr-only">Value stored, hidden. </span>
        }
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Description))
        {
            <span>@Description </span>
        }
        <span class="odc-sfield-stamp">@MetaText</span>
        @* Not an error: the field is not wrong, it is not this caller's to change. *@
        @if (Disabled)
        {
            <span class="odc-sfield-stamp odc-secret-lock">
                <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">lock</span>
                Requires the security settings permission.
            </span>
        }
        @if (Entering && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(_value))
        {
            <span class="odc-secret-note">
                Saved on its own, not with <b>Save changes</b>. Leaving or filtering this field away
                discards what you have typed.
            </span>
        }
        <span class="sr-only"> Settings key @SecretKey.</span>
    </div>

    @* The third helper channel, distinct from Help and Error (CLAUDE.md): non-blocking text about a
       cost, never a fault. Only while the row is NotSet — an absent row is healthy, and an
       undecryptable one belongs to the error channel above. *@
    @if (ConsequenceText is { } consequence)
    {
        <div class="odc-sfield-advisory" id="@AdvisoryId">
            <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">info</span>
            <div><b class="odc-sfield-advisory-t">Advisory</b> @consequence</div>
        </div>
    }
</div>

<OdsSecretClearDialog Open="_confirmOpen"
                      OpenChanged="OnConfirmOpenChanged"
                      Title="@Title"
                      SecretKey="@SecretKey"
                      IsDerivationKey="@IsDerivationKey"
                      Unreadable="@(State == SecretSettingState.Unreadable)"
                      Consequence="@Consequence"
                      Error="@_rowError"
                      OnConfirm="ConfirmClearAsync" />
